<title>USA: Visual holders reject reverse split. [CORRECTED 19:40 GMT]</title>
<headline>Visual holders reject reverse split. [CORRECTED 19:40 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>SOUTH HACKENSACK, N.J. 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Visual Telephone International Inc said Friday shareholders rejected a proposed one-for-ten reverse stock split.</p>
<p>The company proposed the reverse split to shareholders on April 16.</p>
<p>Visual's chief executive Carl Ceragno called the proposal (corrects from &quot;rejection&quot;) &quot;counter-productive in light of the negotiations with investment firms for supplemental capitalization.&quot;</p>
<p>((New York Newsdesk 212 859 1610))</p>
</text>
